config DEVDCS_BOOTSTATE_SPOOF
	bool "Spoof bootloader lock state in /proc/cmdline and ro.boot.*"
	default n
	help
	  Rewrite the verified-boot / lock tokens the bootloader leaves in the
	  kernel command line (verifiedbootstate, vbmeta.device_state,
	  flash.locked, warranty_bit, verifiedbooterror, selinux) to their stock
	  locked values in an early initcall, before init reads them. A software
	  check of /proc/cmdline or the ro.boot.* properties then sees a locked
	  phone.

	  Presentation only: it does not relock anything and does not touch
	  hardware key attestation (Titan M), which still reports the real state -
	  pair it with a valid keybox for that. Lock signals delivered through
	  bootconfig rather than the command line are handled by the companion
	  resetprop step, not here.

	  Compiled out entirely unless set. If unsure, say N.
